NOTE: exact hex/px values below are estimated from a photographed screenshot (camera + compression will have shifted true colors). For pixel-exact fidelity, pull real values via browser devtools getComputedStyle on the actual app before finalizing tokens.

1. COLOR TOKENS

- App background: near-black navy (~#0B1220–#0E1626)
- Tile/panel background: muted slate-blue, lighter than app bg (~#2E3E52–#334459) — tiles read as cards floating on darker canvas
- Check for subtle gradient (lighter top / darker bottom) on tile bg vs flat fill
- Header bar background: darkest navy, near-black, distinct from tile bg
- Primary accent (active tab underline, links, badges, pills): cyan/teal (~#2FD3D9–#4FC7D9)
- Secondary accent (active/selected icon fill, segmented control active state): saturated blue (~#3B82F6) — confirm this is a distinct token from the teal, not the same color
- Primary text: warm off-white/cream, not pure white (large KPI numbers)
- Secondary/label text: light gray-blue (~#9FB0C3)
- Border/divider color: low-contrast gray-blue line, barely visible
- Notification banner background: solid teal/cyan fill (same family as primary accent)
- Notification banner text: white; link text same white, underlined only
- Tooltip background: near-black/charcoal, higher contrast than tile bg
- Tooltip text: white
- Icon default color: muted white/gray
- Icon hover/active: rounded-square background fill in secondary accent blue, icon turns white/high-contrast

2. TYPOGRAPHY

- Font family: clean grotesk/sans (system-ui-like or corporate sans) — pick closest available if source font unidentified
- KPI large numbers: bold, large (~28–36px), tabular/lining figures so digits align
- KPI unit suffix text (e.g. small label after big number): smaller, lighter weight, muted color, baseline-aligned inline to the right
- Tile titles: medium weight, small-medium size, white/cream
- Tab labels: regular weight inactive; active state differentiated by color + underline, not necessarily bold
- Table header text: bold, smaller than tile title, white
- Table cell text: regular weight, slightly muted vs pure white
- Chart axis labels: small, muted gray-blue; x-axis labels may rotate at an angle when space-constrained

3. TILE / PANEL CHROME

- Corner radius: small-medium rounding on all tiles (~6–10px)
- Tile header row: title left, action icon row right, thin horizontal divider below separating header from content
- Header height: compact single line, generous horizontal padding
- Resize handle: small diagonal-lines glyph, bottom-right corner, low-contrast, subtle unless hovered
- Tile hover state: verify whether tile bg lightens or border appears on hover
- Drag state: elevated shadow + slight opacity change + placeholder outline left in original position (standard pattern, infer since not directly visible mid-drag)

4. TABS (page-level and tile-internal)

- Inactive tab: muted gray-blue text, no underline/background
- Active tab: brighter white/cream (or accent) text + thin (~2px) underline bar in teal accent, width = label width only, not full tab-strip width
- Overflow affordance: ">" chevron button when tabs exceed available width (seen on tile-internal tabs) — build as generic "more tabs" control
- Comfortable horizontal spacing between tabs, no vertical separators — color/underline is the only differentiator

5. TOOLBAR ICON ROW (top-right of each tile)

- Icon set: export, download, expand/fullscreen, close — treat as a generic configurable icon-action row
- Default: small, muted white/gray, evenly spaced, minimal internal padding
- Hover/active: rounded-square accent-blue fill appears behind the icon, icon inverts to white, cursor becomes pointer
- Click target padding larger than the glyph itself (hover square bigger than icon)

6. TOOLTIPS

- Trigger: hover over toolbar icon
- Position: adjacent to icon (verify dynamic placement based on available space)
- Background: solid near-black, high contrast vs tile bg
- Text: white, single line, small-medium, medium weight
- Padding: generous, reads as small solid box not thin label
- No arrow/caret pointer nub — plain floating rounded rect
- Corner radius matches general tile radius token

7. NOTIFICATION / SYSTEM BANNER

- Solid teal/cyan fill, docked near top of content, overlaps other UI (elevated z-index, dismissible toast behavior, not part of normal flow)
- Contains: message text (white) + inline underlined link (white, underline only) + dismiss X icon (right, same style as tile close icons)
- Slight corner rounding + soft shadow beneath for elevation separation from content behind

8. FILTER CHIPS / BADGES

- Filter chip: rounded rect, tile-toned dark background, white text, inline "X" remove icon on right, thin border outline
- Status pill/badge (small teal-filled): fully rounded pill shape, solid teal fill, compact padding, small font — verify text contrast (may be dark navy text on teal, distinct from banner's white-on-teal)

9. INPUTS

- Text/search input: rounded rect, thin light border, transparent or slightly-lighter-than-bg fill, muted placeholder text, comfortable left padding, no separate label (placeholder-as-label pattern)
- Input height aligned with toolbar icon row height for visual consistency

10. TABLES

- Header row: bold white text above a thin full-width divider
- Sort indicator: small up/down arrow glyph next to header label, shown on active sorted column (verify whether all sortable columns show muted arrow or only active one)
- Column headers truncate with ellipsis when too narrow — implies user-resizable columns
- No zebra striping visible — rows likely flat, differentiated only on hover (verify)
- Empty state: header shows with blank body, no "no data" message visible in source — decide whether to keep this silent-empty pattern or add a message

11. CHARTS

- Axis lines: thin, muted gray-blue
- Axis labels: small muted text; x-axis month labels may rotate when space-constrained
- Gridlines: minimal-to-none, relies mainly on axis baseline
- Legend: small colored square swatches + label text, bottom-positioned, horizontal layout
- Toggle controls (e.g. time range / chart type switchers): segmented-button group — inactive segments transparent/muted text, active segment gets solid blue fill + white text, grouped as one rounded-rect control

12. SCROLLBARS

- Thin custom scrollbar (not default OS style) — light gray-blue thumb, transparent/invisible track, flush to container edge, only inside scrollable tile content

13. CROSS-CUTTING INTERACTION STATES

- One consistent hover pattern reused everywhere clickable: rounded-square accent-blue fill + icon color inversion (toolbar icons, banner dismiss, filter chip remove, etc.)
- Consistent keyboard focus-ring style using accent-blue token (not visible in source, required for a11y-complete replication)
- Pointer/hand cursor on every clickable target, not just some

14. ELEVATION / SHADOWS

- Tiles: little-to-no shadow against dark bg — differentiation mainly via background color contrast, keep flat
- Banner/toast: slightly more elevation than tiles — subtle shadow since it floats above content

